            <ArticleTitle>The Pyrenoid: An Overlooked Organelle Comes out of Age.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>28-29</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0092-8674(17)31061-9</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cell.2017.09.012</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The pyrenoid is a membrane-less organelle that exists in various photosynthetic organisms, such as algae, and wherein most global CO2 fixation occurs. Two papers from the Jonikas lab in this issue of Cell provide new insights into the structure, protein composition, and dynamics of this important organelle.</AbstractText>
